        "t1": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABIivD8Q",
            "number": 1599,
            "title": "fix(static): normalize indexNames path join with single boundary slash",
            "body": "<!--\nThank you for reporting an issue.\n\nThe issue tracker is for reporting bugs and discussing features.\n-->\n\n### 🔗 Linked issue\n\nCloses #1584\n\n### ❓ Type of change\n\n- [x] 📖 Documentation (updates to the documentation, readme or JSdoc annotations)\n- [x] 🐞 Bug fix (a non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] 👌 Enhancement (improving an existing functionality like performance)\n- [ ] ✨ New feature (a non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] 🧹 Chore (updates to the build process or auxiliary tools and libraries)\n- [ ] ⚠️ Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to change)\n\n### 📚 Description\n\nWhen serving static index files, `idSearchPaths` previously constructed candidate asset IDs by simple string concatenation: `${id}${suffix}`.\n\nBecause `originalId` for root `GET /` retains a leading slash (`withoutTrailingSlash(\"/\") === \"/\"`):\n1. **Root double slash with default `indexNames: [\"/index.html\"]`**:\n   Concatenating `\"/\"` and `\"/index.html\"` resulted in `\"//index.html\"`. This non-canonical path fails canonical path lookup and asset table lookup in storage backends, returning a `404` for root index requests.\n2. **Missing directory separator with relative `indexNames: [\"index.html\"]`**:\n   When configuring relative index names without a leading slash, requesting a subdirectory like `GET /docs` concatenated `\"/docs\"` and `\"index.html\"`, producing `\"/docsindex.html\"`.\n\nThis fix normalizes index name boundary joining:\n```ts\nconst assetId = suffix ? `${id.replace(/\\/+$/, \"\")}/${suffix.replace(/^\\/+/, \"\")}` : id;\n```\nEnsuring a single slash boundary regardless of whether `id` is `\"/\"` or a subdirectory, and whether `suffix` contains a leading slash.\n\n### 📝 Checklist\n\n- [x] I have linked an issue or discussion.\n- [x] I have updated the documentation accordingly.\n- [x] I have added tests to cover my changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Fixed static asset lookup paths so root and directory index requests resolve correctly when paths contain leading or trailing slashes.\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for index resolution at the root and in subdirectories.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
