        "t2": {
          "issueOrPullRequest": {
            "__typename": "PullRequest",
            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABISBMpA",
            "number": 1598,
            "title": "fix(static): normalize directory-index path join in idSearchPaths (#1584)",
            "body": "### Summary\n\nFixes #1584.\n\nIn `src/utils/static.ts`, `idSearchPaths` previously concatenated candidate asset IDs directly with `${id}${suffix}`.\nBecause root requests normalize to `id = \"/\"`:\n1. When using the default `indexNames: [\"/index.html\"]`, requesting root `GET /` produced candidate asset ID `\"//index.html\"`. For backends keyed by canonical asset paths, looking up `\"//index.html\"` fails with 404.\n2. When configuring relative index names such as `indexNames: [\"index.html\"]`, subdirectory requests like `GET /docs` produced `\"/docsindex.html\"` due to a missing boundary slash.\n\nThis change normalizes `assetId` join boundaries in `idSearchPaths` so that:\n- Root `GET /` with `\"/index.html\"` or `\"index.html\"` maps to `\"/index.html\"`.\n- Subdirectory `GET /docs` with `\"/index.html\"` or `\"index.html\"` maps to `\"/docs/index.html\"`.\n\nUnit tests covering root and subdirectory lookups with both absolute and relative index names have been added in `test/static.test.ts`.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Fixed static index-file lookup paths to handle root and subdirectory IDs without missing or duplicated separators. Non-index paths remain unchanged.\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for serving index files from the root and subdirectories with absolute and relative index names.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
            "state": "OPEN",
            "isDraft": false,
